GREEN. claude-launcher.ts 174 -> 190 lines (under 250).

Three edits, all inside `launchClaude`'s existing ordering:
1. Import: `validateRuntimeBinding` and `type RuntimeBindingCheck` added to the EXISTING `../../supervisor/effect-grant.js` import (wrapped to two lines).
2. `PHASE` gained a DISTINCT entry `binding: "the prepared runtime is not the runtime this activation committed"`. `PHASE.activation` was NOT reused — its text names the activation-commit authority and would misdescribe a runtime mismatch. The new message names no digest, no path, no identifier.
3. The guard sits immediately AFTER the commit phase's OK/MALFORMED handling and immediately BEFORE the grant phase:
   let bound: RuntimeBindingCheck;
   try { bound = validateRuntimeBinding(request.effect, runtime.value.quotedObservationDigest); }
   catch { return directFailure("CLAUDE_LAUNCH_DEPENDENCY_THROWN", "ACTIVATION", PHASE.binding); }
   if (bound.kind === "REFUSED") return directFailure(bound.failure.code, bound.failure.layer, PHASE.binding);

Operand: `runtime.value.quotedObservationDigest`, NEVER `freshObservationDigest` — the fresh digest covers the RE-OBSERVED PINNED closure whose entry paths live under the pin root, so it can never equal the quote and would refuse every correct launch. The matched happy-path test asserting `COMMIT.intent.runtimeObservationDigest === prepared.quotedObservationDigest` and reaching OBSERVED is the live proof the right operand was chosen.

Containment: `validateRuntimeBinding` is a direct import, not an injected port, so nothing else on that path holds a `try`. The explicit try/catch maps a throw to CLAUDE_LAUNCH_DEPENDENCY_THROWN at ACTIVATION, preserving the launcher's total-result invariant (the public promise can never reject). `contained()` was not reused: it exists to decode HOSTILE port results, and this callee is our own pure function whose union arms are already typed.

No new code minted: `SupervisorErrorCode` and `SupervisorLayer` are already spread into CLAUDE_LAUNCH_ERROR_CODES / CLAUDE_LAUNCH_LAYERS (claude-launcher-contract.ts:21,24), so `bound.failure.code` and `.layer` typecheck straight into `directFailure` and pass through untranslated. No contract change.

